Tell it the session identifier and our host key blob once the transport is established (gf_conn_info).  Starts the grace time.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_server_input\fP (gf_auth_server *a, uint64_t now_us, const uint8_t *payload, size_t len);
A message numbered 50 to 79 from the client.  Returns GF_OK, or an error after which the machine has asked for the connection to be ended.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_server_accept\fP (gf_auth_server *a, uint64_t now_us);
.br
int \fBgf_auth_server_reject\fP (gf_auth_server *a, uint64_t now_us, int partial_success);
.br
int \fBgf_auth_server_pk_ok\fP (gf_auth_server *a, uint64_t now_us);
Answers.  Each is valid once, after a request.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_server_kbdint_prompt\fP (gf_auth_server *a, uint64_t now_us, const char *name, const char *instruction, size_t nprompts, const char *const *prompts, const int *echo);
Ask the client NPROMPTS questions.  PROMPTS are NUL\-terminated UTF\-8; ECHO says which answers may be shown as typed.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_server_banner\fP (gf_auth_server *a, uint64_t now_us, const char *text);
Send a banner (RFC 4252 section 5.4), UTF\-8 and without control characters.  Allowed before success.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_server_force_command\fP (const gf_auth_server *a, gf_slice *cmd);
After the authenticated event for a user who presented a certificate: its force\-command (NUL\-terminated; *CMD is empty if it has none).  The command is valid until the machine is freed.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_server_permits\fP (const gf_auth_server *a, const char *permission);
After the authenticated event: does the user's certificate permit PERMISSION, one of the extensions of key.h ("permit\-pty" and the like)? 1 if the user did not authenticate with a certificate, since there is then nothing that restricts them, and for any other key type.
.TP
uint64_t \fBgf_auth_server_timeout\fP (const gf_auth_server *a);
.br
int \fBgf_auth_server_on_timeout\fP (gf_auth_server *a, uint64_t now_us);
.br
int \fBgf_auth_server_is_done\fP (const gf_auth_server *a);
