int \fBgf_auth_client_extension\fP (gf_auth_client *a, gf_slice name, gf_slice value);
The server's extensions (RFC 8308), from the transport's extension event: "server\-sig\-algs" limits the RSA hash the client uses, and "publickey\-hostbound@openssh.com" switches to the host\-bound method. Others are ignored.  Call before start.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_client_start\fP (gf_auth_client *a, uint64_t now_us, const uint8_t *session_id, size_t session_id_len, const uint8_t *host_key_blob, size_t host_key_len);
Begin: the session identifier and the host key blob of the connection (gf_conn_info), and send the first request.  Call once the service request was accepted.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_client_input\fP (gf_auth_client *a, uint64_t now_us, const uint8_t *payload, size_t len);
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_client_kbdint_respond\fP (gf_auth_client *a, uint64_t now_us, size_t n, const char *const *responses);
Answer keyboard\-interactive prompts: one response per prompt.
.TP
int \fBgf_auth_client_sign_respond\fP (gf_auth_client *a, uint64_t now_us, const uint8_t *sig, size_t len);
.br
int \fBgf_auth_client_sign_fail\fP (gf_auth_client *a, uint64_t now_us);
Answer the sign event: the signature blob, or that there is none. GF_ERR_STATE if nothing was asked.  A signature that does not verify as KEY's for the data (or whose token was not touched) skips the key as a failure would.
